From: damnbitimcrit <333091414+damnbitimcrit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Halo 3] Name the signed-in profile as the content author;
 log film desyncs

Halo 3 writes the author of a film, clip, screenshot or map or game
variant (sub_821E8A58, the content metadata) only for a profile signed in
to Xbox Live: the gamertag the game keeps in the player's slot
(slot+0x990). Xenia signs profiles in locally, so everything made in
Xenia had no author, as on a console with an offline profile.

- halo3_author_from_profile (default on): hook 821E8B48 (once the
  author's name source r26 is chosen; reached from 821E8B40 and by
  fall-through from 821E8B44): if r26 is still the empty name, the slot
  r30 is one of the four user slots and isn't a player without a profile
  (flag 0x4, which has a random name), and its gamertag isn't empty,
  point r26 at it, as the Live path does. The XUID and the online flag
  are left as the game sets them.
- Theater film desync log: hook 820A4268 (sub_820A4098, reached only by
  falling through after a recorded update didn't match) logs the updates
  played, the film mode, and the recorded and current film tick, game
  tick and random seed, once per film; hook 823BD140 (entry, five calls)
  logs a film stopped because it couldn't be read or decoded (reason 0).
---
 src/xenia/kernel/title/halo3/halo3.cc         |   1 +
 src/xenia/kernel/title/halo3/halo3.h          |   2 +
 src/xenia/kernel/title/halo3/halo3_content.cc | 199 ++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 202 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 src/xenia/kernel/title/halo3/halo3_content.cc

diff --git a/src/xenia/kernel/title/halo3/halo3.cc b/src/xenia/kernel/title/halo3/halo3.cc
index b08e8e8..752497b 100644
--- a/src/xenia/kernel/title/halo3/halo3.cc
+++ b/src/xenia/kernel/title/halo3/halo3.cc
@@ -735,6 +735,7 @@ void Install(KernelState* kernel_state, UserModule* module) {
   InstallInput(kernel_state);
   InstallTiming(kernel_state);
   InstallTheaterSnapshots(kernel_state);
+  InstallContent(kernel_state);
   auto& hooks = cpu::GuestHooks::Get();
   auto processor = kernel_state->processor();
   hooks.Add(processor, kMainLoopBodyEntry, OnMainLoopBodyEntry);
diff --git a/src/xenia/kernel/title/halo3/halo3.h b/src/xenia/kernel/title/halo3/halo3.h
index cd9711d..a9ce046 100644
--- a/src/xenia/kernel/title/halo3/halo3.h
+++ b/src/xenia/kernel/title/halo3/halo3.h
@@ -179,6 +179,8 @@ void InstallTiming(KernelState* kernel_state);
 void InstallInput(KernelState* kernel_state);
 // halo3_theater.cc
 void InstallTheaterSnapshots(KernelState* kernel_state);
+// halo3_content.cc
+void InstallContent(KernelState* kernel_state);
 // Takes the mouse motion for this frame.
 void OnInputFrameStart(cpu::ppc::PPCContext* ctx);
 
diff --git a/src/xenia/kernel/title/halo3/halo3_content.cc b/src/xenia/kernel/title/halo3/halo3_content.cc
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..08b9f47
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/xenia/kernel/title/halo3/halo3_content.cc
@@ -0,0 +1,199 @@
+/**
+ ******************************************************************************
+ * Xenia : Xbox 360 Emulator Research Project                                 *
